From 7104f2f4a3f481ae3f733cd5b4c4e5299237594c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Spooren <mail@aparcar.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] netlink: specs: rt-link: add bpdu-filter

710-bridge-add-knob-for-filtering-rx-tx-BPDU-pack.patch adds
IFLA_BRPORT_BPDU_FILTER (45) to the bridge port attributes, but not to
the rt-link netlink spec. YNL users (ynl cli, the drivers/net Python
selftests) then fail to decode any RTM_GETLINK reply of a bridge port
with "Space 'linkinfo-brport-attrs' has no attribute with value '45'",
e.g. drivers/net/stats.py on the LAN port of an OpenWrt One.

Signed-off-by: Paul Spooren <mail@aparcar.org>
---
 Documentation/netlink/specs/rt-link.yaml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/Documentation/netlink/specs/rt-link.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/netlink/specs/rt-link.yaml
@@ -1689,6 +1689,9 @@ attribute-sets:
       -
         name: backup-nhid
         type: u32
+      -
+        name: bpdu-filter
+        type: u8
   -
     name: linkinfo-gre-attrs
     name-prefix: ifla-gre-
